# args: -O0 --eval=':disasm 1+2'
# The constant pool holds one entry more than the code references: the
# prompt compiles through the same .jaic container every module does, and
# the container stores a function's name in its pool. It was absent while
# the prompt compiled straight to an ObjFunction and never serialised.
# The optimisation level on the command line configures the evaluator behind
# --eval, not just the one behind `repl`: at -O0 the two operands are still
# there to be added at run time, where the default folds them to a 3.
print("stdin was read")
